# Duration multiplication beyond machine integers

The components of durations are machine integers in the OCaml, C and Java
runtimes: the product is the IntegerOverflow runtime error there, not a
wrapped or truncated duration. Python integers are unbounded.

> Module Overflow

```catala-metadata
#[test]
declaration scope Mult:
  output d content duration
```

```catala
scope Mult:
  definition d equals 2 day * 9223372036854775807
```
